WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568
-Your son is coming up on
his second birthday, right?

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Second birthday.
Same age as your guy.

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:05.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep, same as mine.
And you --

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:06.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know you have to do
a lot of press

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you're promoting shows,
press like this,

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
which must be exhausting
with a 2-year-old.

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:12.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. So, like, the big
difference between

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:14.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
when we started the show
and six years later,

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:16.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
we do very similar
kind of press things.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:20.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, six years ago,
we would've been, you know,

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
meeting between
each press event

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:23.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
and drinking massive
amounts of wine,

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, like, making out
in a bathroom somewhere.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:26.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Great.
-Okay.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:28.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's awesome.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This year,
the exact same schedule,

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
exact same press event, we --
I'm not joking --

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:35.135 line:92%
asked our driver, in between,

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:39.172
to not only not go to have
drinks and make-out places,

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.473 line:92%
we said, "Can you pull over?

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
And can we take a nap
in the car?"

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:44.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"What has our life come to?"

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:47.781
A nap? In our fancy clothes
just like this in the car.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:50.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nothing would be more
terrifying than walking by

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
and seeing the cast of
"The Americans"

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.320 line:92%
asleep in the back of a car.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd be like, "Oh, no!
They're dead!"

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"They're dead."
I know.

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:01.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Spoiler alert --
they die in a car.

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:02.595 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:03.430 size:88% position:44% line:92%
They fully die in a car.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They looked nice,
but they're dead.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Matthew is Welsh.
-He's Welsh.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And is he speaking Welsh
with the baby?

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.740
-He is. So, he speaks --
Welsh is his first language

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.942 line:92%
and speaks exclusively in Welsh.

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:21.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we, as a family,
all learn colors, numbers...

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.383 line:92%
yeah, and that's how we do.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:27.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How is --
Is a baby speaking Welsh cute?

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very.
-Okay.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:30.323
'Cause it's a pretty --
It's, like, an intense language.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:31.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's an intense language.
-Yeah.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:34.828
-He does a very good job,
and it is -- it's amazing.

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:37.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he's sort of tri-lingual,
because we also have

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.699 size:75% position:38%
someone in our house
who speaks Spanish.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.267 size:78% position:39% line:92%
So we do like chww --

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.904
-How do you say, like,
"mother" and "father" in Welsh?

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, he just says
mama and dada.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:49.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, well,
so he's not crushing it?

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.645 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:53.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not yet.
-Not yet.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:54.948 line:92%
Well, he's got plenty of time.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:58.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I do want to ask, like,
did you know it before

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you had --
before you had a 2-year-old?

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was there any reason
for you guys to speak Welsh

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:03.857 size:81% position:41%
up until that point?
-I spoke a little bit.

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:05.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean his family,
when he calls home,

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:08.228
when he speaks to his sister
on the phone, he speaks Welsh.

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:11.931
So now I can say, "What are
we doing at 4:00 on Tuesday?"

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:14.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, and he'll go,
"Oh, she's learning too much."

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what I mean?
-Oh!

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:17.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now, though --
Like, you guys can now --

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
You kind of have
your own spy language now.

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:19.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which is kind of amazing.
Yeah.

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:23.176
-So, like, if you guys were out,
like, walking the streets,

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:24.410 line:92%
you could do a little Welsh?

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.245 line:92%
-You could do a little Welsh,

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:27.714
and you could talk some serious
[bleep] about people.

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow. Is Welsh
a good language for that?

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:33.219
They have a lot of [bleep] talk?
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:36.189 size:84% position:42%
-Are you -- So, are you
bittersweet about it?

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:37.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must feel like
such an accomplishment

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:40.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
to finish this show
that was so well received

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:42.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
and beloved
by the people who watched it.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:42.829 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It is.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, personally,
it was such a great job.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a really,
really great job,

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:50.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, obviously,
I had some huge life changes

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:53.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
connected with it,
but at the same time,

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're kind of --
we're not out of it yet.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:55.742 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:58.211 size:88% position:44%
-I'm still celebrating
the fact that, you know,

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:59.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm out, I'm free.
-Right.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which is so --
I feel like I just

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
got out of school,
and I'm going for, like,

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
lunch by myself,
which feels amazing!

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:07.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which may seem
really boring to you,

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
but lunch by myself
feels amazing

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:12.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
and not with 200, you know,
crew members.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:12.659 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:16.863
Also you get to dress in, like,
decade-appropriate clothing.

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:17.864 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:19.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is also true.
-Yeah.

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:20.433 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-This is also true.

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:24.437
Not a lot of wig wearing or,
you know, 1980s eye shadow.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:26.539 line:92%
-Well, I cannot congratulate you

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:27.707 size:78% position:39%
and everyone involved
in the show enough.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's always just
such a delight to see you.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please do come back again.
-Okay, fine!.

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:32.145 line:92%
-It wasn't your last time here.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.948 size:88% position:44%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Keri Russell, everybody!

